// expect-ok
// Z3 corpus #29: axis-1 — Wall 4 Step 2 refinement preservation through field reads (positive evidence).
//
// WHAT THIS FIXTURE PROVES
//
// Wall 4 Step 2 lets refinements travel through `TypedExprKind::FieldAccess`.
// When `idx.value` is read from a refined source record, the resulting
// `TypedExpr` carries the source record's matching refinement clauses
// as a Vec<RefinementClause>. The construction-site dispatcher then
// accepts the symbolic value when at least one supplied clause
// structurally matches each destination clause (V11 + V14 syntactic
// equality, ∃-quantified match per destination clause).
//
// V23 invariant: source and destination records have DISTINCT names
// (Index vs Mirror) to prove the match path works across records, not
// just same-named-self-copy. Field names also differ (value vs copy)
// to prove `refinements_match` ignores field names per V2.
//
// THE LANGUAGE PRIMITIVES THIS NEEDED
//
//   * Step 1's where-clause grammar + Z3 satisfiability dispatch.
//   * Step 2's `refinement: Option<Vec<RefinementClause>>` field on
//     TypedExpr (V16 storage shape).
//   * `infer_field_access_expr` attaches refinement when field_ty is
//     i64 (V18 gate) and the source record has clauses matching the
//     accessed field name (V16 collect-all-matching).
//   * `check_record_refinements_at_construction` dispatcher's
//     symbolic-with-match path (V3 step 2; V11 Z3-SKIP).
//   * `refinements_match` helper (V2 + V14 + V17) comparing ONLY
//     (op, literal); field names dropped.
//
// MUTATION CONTRACT
//
// Not applicable (this is the positive-evidence fixture). Changing
// Mirror's `where copy >= 0` to `where copy > 0` would flip the
// dispatcher into the T215 branch (fixture #31). Removing both
// `where` clauses drops both records' refinement obligations and
// the program still compiles.
module sigil;

record Index { value: i64 } where value >= 0

record Mirror { copy: i64 } where copy >= 0

entry actor Main {
    on Tick() -> i64 {
        let idx: Index = Index { value: 42 };
        let m: Mirror = Mirror { copy: idx.value };
        return 1;
    }
}
